# SnapShop v2 — CLIP + FAISS (No SerpApi Needed)

Reverse image shopping using **OpenAI CLIP** + **Meta FAISS** running on your local GPU.
Zero external API dependencies. Zero CORS issues. Zero cost per search.

---

## How It Works

```
User uploads photo
       ↓
CLIP (ViT-B-32) encodes image → 512-dim vector
       ↓
FAISS searches indexed product vectors (cosine similarity)
       ↓
Top-K most similar products returned with scores
       ↓
Frontend shows products with prices + buy links
```

---

## Setup — 4 Steps

### Step 1 — Install dependencies

```bash
# Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate      # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate

# Install (CUDA GPU version)
pip install torch torchvision --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu118
pip install faiss-gpu open-clip-torch Pillow requests
pip install fastapi uvicorn[standard] python-multipart pydantic pydantic-settings

# CPU-only (slower but works anywhere)
pip install torch torchvision
pip install faiss-cpu open-clip-torch Pillow requests
pip install fastapi uvicorn[standard] python-multipart pydantic pydantic-settings
```

### Step 2 — Build the FAISS index (run ONCE)

```bash
python scripts/build_index.py
```

Expected output:
```
Building FAISS index for 20 products…
  Indexed 10/20 products…
  Indexed 20/20 products…
Index built: 20 vectors | 0 skipped
✅ Index built successfully!
   Products indexed : 20
   Time taken       : 12.3s
   Saved to         : data/products.faiss
```

### Step 3 — Test it works

```bash
# Test with a sneaker image
python scripts/test_search.py --url https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1542291026-7eec264c27ff

# Test text search (CLIP superpower)
python scripts/test_search.py --text "red ethnic kurta women"
```

### Step 4 — Start the backend

```bash
uvicorn backend.main:app --reload

# You'll see:
# ✅ CLIP + FAISS ready. Server is accepting requests.
# INFO: Uvicorn running on http://0.0.0.0:8000
```

---

## API Endpoints

| Endpoint | Method | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `/health` | GET | Check CLIP + FAISS status |
| `/api/search/upload` | POST | Upload image file → find similar |
| `/api/search/url` | POST | Image URL → find similar |
| `/api/search/text` | POST | Text query → find similar |
| `/api/catalog/stats` | GET | Index stats |
| `/api/catalog/products` | GET | All indexed products |
| `/api/catalog/rebuild` | POST | Rebuild index from catalog.json |
| `/docs` | GET | Swagger UI (test endpoints) |

---

## Test via Swagger UI

Go to http://localhost:8000/docs
Click "Try it out" on any endpoint — no auth needed.

---

## Add More Products

Edit `data/catalog.json` — add entries like:

```json
{
  "id": "MY_PRODUCT_001",
  "title": "Product Name",
  "price": "₹999",
  "platform": "Amazon India",
  "category": "fashion",
  "buy_url": "https://amazon.in/...",
  "image_url": "https://example.com/product.jpg",
  "thumbnail": "https://example.com/product-thumb.jpg"
}
```

Then rebuild:
```bash
python scripts/build_index.py --force
```

Or call the API:
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/catalog/rebuild
```

---

## Frontend

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
# → http://localhost:3000
```

---

## Why CLIP + FAISS > SerpApi

| Feature | SerpApi | CLIP + FAISS |
|---|---|---|
| Cost | $75/mo for 5K searches | $0 after setup |
| CORS issues | Yes (needs backend proxy) | No |
| Offline | No | Yes |
| Speed | ~2000ms | ~50ms on GPU |
| Control | None | Full |
| Indian catalog | Whatever Google indexes | Your own catalog |
| Text search | No | Yes (CLIP is multimodal) |
